Origin
------

DebPlus is derived from butterknife, an archinstall-style TUI installer for
Debian 13 created by the Butterbian project (JustAGuyLinux):

    https://justaguy.dev/drew/butterknife

butterknife is licensed under GPL-2.0. The files below are derived from it and
retain its copyright notice:

    installer/app.py
    installer/screens.py
    installer/widgets.py
    installer/installer.py
    installer/utils.py

Parts of the build approach and the Debian package lists also come from
butterknife's build-iso.sh and build-rootfs.sh.

Changes from butterknife
------------------------

The following are new in DebPlus, or substantially changed from butterknife:

- Window managers and desktops are data files (options/wms.list, options/desktops.list), not a
  hardcoded bash chooser.
- Optional menus (Packages, Hardware, Software, Advanced) are driven by list
  files (options/components.list, options/extras.list, packages/firmware.list).
- Wi-Fi scanning, connection, and a connection test against the Debian mirror, and profiles are copied into the installed system.
- Filesystem options are modified.
- The installer reboots automatically after a successful install.
- Configuration is in plain-text list files and profile.env, and the project
  is branded as DebPlus.
- Added --test option to installer for safer testing.

Third-party software
--------------------

DebPlus installs Debian packages and window manager repositories at install
time. Those packages and repositories keep their own licenses. Check each one
before redistribution.
